(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_chemistry_thesblockelements=[{id:"neet-2023-q059",pn:59,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"The s-Block Elements",st:"Biological importance of Mg and Ca",q:"Which one of the following statements is correct ?",o:["Mg plays roles in neuromuscular function and interneuronal transmission","The daily requirement of Mg and Ca in the human body is estimated to be 0.2 \u2013 0.3 g.","All enzymes that utilise ATP in phosphate transfer require Ca as the cofactor","The bone in human body is an inert and unchanging substance"],c:1,s:`Ca (not Mg) plays the role in neuromuscular function and interneuronal transmission, so option 1 is wrong.
The daily need of Mg and Ca is about 200\u2013300 mg (0.2\u20130.3 g), so option 2 is correct.
Enzymes using ATP for phosphate transfer need Mg as the cofactor, not Ca, so option 3 is wrong.
Bone is not inert; it is continually dissolved and redeposited, so option 4 is wrong.`},{id:"neet-2023-q079",pn:79,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"The s-Block Elements",st:"Alkali metals in liquid ammonia",q:`Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R :
Assertion A : Metallic sodium dissolves in liquid ammonia giving a deep blue solution, which is paramagnetic.
Reason R : The deep blue solution is due to the formation of amide.
In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["A is false but R is true","Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.","Both A and R are true and R is NOT the correct explanation of A.","A is true but R is false."],c:3,s:`Sodium in liquid ammonia gives M + (x + y)NH\u2083 \u2192 [M(NH\u2083)\u2093]\u207A + [e(NH\u2083)\u1D67]\u207B.
The ammoniated electron absorbs visible light, which gives the deep blue colour.
The unpaired electron makes the solution paramagnetic.
So A is true, but R is false because the colour is not due to amide.`}]})();
